<h1>Smart Class Attendance System</h1>
<p><strong>Comprehensive Project Documentation & Technical Specification</strong></p>
<p><em>Generated on: June 2026</em></p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">Executive Summary</div>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">The <strong>Smart Class Attendance System</strong> is a state-of-the-art, web-based institutional platform designed to automate student attendance tracking while completely eliminating proxy marking. Combining real-time GPS geofencing, hardware biometric authentication (WebAuthn), dynamic classroom OTP PINs, and device fingerprint locks, the system ensures high accuracy, security, and effortless classroom management.</p>
</div>

<h2>1. System Architecture & Technology Stack</h2>
<p>The application is built upon a modern, decoupled single-page application (SPA) architecture designed for high performance, visual excellence, and seamless operation across desktops, tablets, and mobile devices.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Layer / Module</th>
      <th style="width: 35%;">Technologies Used</th>
      <th style="width: 40%;">Key Responsibilities</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frontend Core</strong></td>
      <td>React 18, Vite, React Router DOM</td>
      <td>Client-side routing, state management, component modularity, and responsive layouts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>UI & Styling Design</strong></td>
      <td>Tailwind CSS, Vanilla CSS tokens, Lucide Icons</td>
      <td>Glassmorphic UI components, smooth animations, status badges, and professional typography.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Biometrics & Vision</strong></td>
      <td><code>react-webcam</code>, <code>face-api.js</code>, WebAuthn API</td>
      <td>Live webcam capture, facial detection models, and hardware fingerprint scanner integration.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Geofencing Engine</strong></td>
      <td>HTML5 Geolocation API, Haversine Formula</td>
      <td>Real-time GPS coordinate extraction and spatial distance validation against classroom radius.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Backend & Persistence</strong></td>
      <td>Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB / LocalStorage</td>
      <td>RESTful API verification endpoints, offline fallbacks, and persistent local data storage.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Multi-Portal Functional Breakdown</h2>
<p>The project is structured into three dedicated role-based portals tailored to specific administrative and academic responsibilities:</p>

<h3>A. Administrator Portal</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Geofence Configuration:</strong> Administrators can establish the physical classroom boundaries by setting exact Latitude and Longitude GPS coordinates and defining an allowable radius (e.g., 500 meters). Includes a convenient <em>"Fetch My Current Location"</em> tool.</li>
  <li><strong>Faculty & Subject Roster:</strong> Complete lifecycle management for teachers. Admins can register faculty members, assign unique Teacher IDs and credentials, and allocate multiple subjects (e.g., <em>Computer Networks, Artificial Intelligence</em>).</li>
  <li><strong>White-Label Branding:</strong> Institutional customization allowing administrators to update the University Name, Department Title, and upload official logos.</li>
  <li><strong>Analytics & Export:</strong> Real-time overview of total registered students, daily attendance figures, and a one-click <strong>CSV Export</strong> tool for Excel reporting and auditing.</li>
</ul>

<h3>B. Teacher Portal</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Subject Attendance Filtering:</strong> Teachers can switch between their assigned subjects to view real-time attendance rosters and student verification statuses.</li>
  <li><strong>Attendance Session Control:</strong> Teachers have full control over when attendance can be marked via a live <strong>Turn ON / Turn OFF</strong> session toggle. Students cannot submit attendance unless the teacher actively opens the session.</li>
  <li><strong>Dynamic Classroom Live PIN (OTP):</strong> When a session is turned on, a dynamic 4-digit security PIN is generated. Teachers display this PIN on the classroom whiteboard. The portal allows teachers to <strong>click into the box to type a custom PIN</strong> or click <strong>"Randomize"</strong> to generate a fresh code.</li>
  <li><strong>Manual Attendance Override:</strong> Enables teachers to manually record attendance for students experiencing technical issues (such as mobile camera failure or low battery), with built-in duplicate validation.</li>
</ul>

<h3>C. Student Portal & Verification Workflow</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Personalized Dashboard:</strong> Students log in using their unique Roll Number to review historical attendance records, track total days present, and monitor overall attendance percentages.</li>
  <li><strong>Guided Verification Funnel:</strong> A clear, step-by-step interactive verification screen that guides students through GPS check, PIN entry, biometric scan, and webcam face capture.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Triple-Layer Anti-Proxy & Security Protocol</h2>
<p>To eliminate proxy attendance—where students mark attendance on behalf of absent peers—the system enforces a rigorous multi-layered verification funnel:</p>

<table style="margin-top: 15px;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Security Layer</th>
      <th style="width: 75%;">Mechanism & Protection Guaranteed</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Device Fingerprint Lock</strong></td>
      <td>Registers a unique hardware token for each student's device. Once a phone or laptop marks attendance for a Roll Number, it is locked for the day. If another student logs in on the same device, submission is blocked with an Anti-Proxy alert.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Classroom Whiteboard PIN</strong></td>
      <td>Requires students to enter the dynamic 4-digit code displayed on the classroom whiteboard. This ensures that students who are nearby (within GPS radius but outside the lecture hall) cannot mark attendance remotely.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Hardware Biometric Scan</strong></td>
      <td>Utilizes the browser's native WebAuthn API to trigger physical hardware sensors (fingerprint scanners, Windows Hello, TouchID, Android Biometrics), verifying the physical user before submission.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. GPS Geofencing Check</strong></td>
      <td>Calculates the exact distance in meters between the student's mobile GPS and the registered classroom coordinates. Submission is disabled if the student is outside the authorized boundary.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>5. Single Attendance Enforcement</strong></td>
      <td>Enforces strict database and local checks preventing a student from marking attendance more than once per subject per day. Subsequent attempts display a confirmation badge and disable submission.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Workflow Summary</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Pre-Class Setup:</strong> The Administrator sets the classroom GPS location and assigns subjects to the Teacher.</li>
  <li><strong>Starting Class:</strong> The Teacher logs into the Teacher Portal, selects the subject, and clicks <strong>"Turn ON Attendance Marking"</strong>. A dynamic 4-digit PIN appears on screen, which the teacher writes on the whiteboard.</li>
  <li><strong>Student Verification:</strong> Students log in on their phones, select the open subject, verify their GPS location, enter the 4-digit whiteboard PIN, complete their hardware biometric/fingerprint scan, and verify their face via webcam.</li>
  <li><strong>Record Locking:</strong> Upon success, the system records the attendance, locks the mobile device from being used for any other student today, and blocks duplicate entries.</li>
</ol>

